# devices/pclm10/drivers/wifi/conf: this phone's first look at its SLPI, the subsystem the WLAN's
# firmware runs on (notes/wifi.md §2). The common drivers/wifi/ is the WCN6750 phone's whole
# Wi-Fi stack and needs fw-wifi/ and QMI; this is one driver of observation: the four power rails
# the icnss node asks for, voted through RPMh, and the Q6's control block, read once.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver SLPI
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.slpi.c
	help    the SLPI of this phone: its rails, its image, and its Q6 block. slpi=1 lists every
	help    resource the boot loader's command database holds, by name and address; slpi=2 adds
	help    the four rails the icnss node asks for (ldoa1 752 mV, ldoa7 1800 mV, ldoc2 1304 mV,
	help    ldoc11 3104 mV, three TCS votes each, the way the touch driver votes ldoa17) and a
	help    report on the two ARC resources the ssc node's vdd_cx and vdd_mx are (named, not
	help    written); slpi=3 adds M2: on a thread that waits for the root, /fw/slpi.mdt and its
	help    segment files are read, handed to TrustZone for their signature, placed in the region
	help    the device tree reserves (0x98100000, 20 MiB, the image shifted by 0xE00000 as the
	help    vendor's relocating loader does), written and read back, and started through the
	help    always-on processor and TrustZone, then the q6 block at 0x5c00000 is read after
	help    slpi_wait seconds (3); slpi=4 reads that block even when the start failed; slpi=5
	help    leaves the always-on processor's mailbox alone and asks TrustZone directly, a
	help    diagnostic for when the mailbox itself is what stops the run. The q6
	help    read is tied to these levels because the phone answered on 2026-11-03
	help    (logs/095451-run.log): while the slpi is down the first read of that window never
	help    comes back and the kernel hangs where it stands -- the block is worth reading only
	help    after something has started the subsystem. slpi_base= overrides the region's address.
	help    No vote here is ever dropped.
